# AppShots frontend design

Follow the project skill at `.cursor/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` (Anthropic). Also apply these product rules.

## Product brief

AppShots makes **store listing assets** in the browser: App Store / Play screenshots **and** Play feature graphics (1024×500). Audience: indie / mobile marketers shipping listings. Vernacular: device frames, store consoles, clean marketing type — not crypto SaaS, not newspaper, not “AI dashboard”.

## Hard avoid (AI-default cluster)

- Warm cream + terracotta/serif combo
- Near-black + acid lime / vermilion as the only accent
- Broadsheet hairlines / zero radius / dense columns
- Identical card kits with soft grey shadows everywhere
- ALL-CAPS eyebrows, middle-dot meta rows, “WORD — fragment”, trailing `→` on every CTA
- Purple-on-white / purple mesh as default theme

## Composition

- First viewport = **one** composition: brand, one headline, one supporting line, one CTA group, one dominant visual
- No stats strips, pill clusters, or secondary marketing in the hero
- No floating badges/stickers on hero media
- Cards only when they contain an interaction; never in the hero
- One job per section

## AppShots tokens (landing)

- Ink: `#070B14` · Surface: `#121826` · Mist: `#9AA4B2` · Paper: `#F4F6FA` · Accent: `#3B82F6` (cobalt, not neon)
- Type: **Sora** (display + UI). No Inter/Roboto/Arial as design choice.
- Logo: wordmark + aperture monogram (`BrandMark`) — keep brand as a hero-level signal

## Editor chrome

Preserve the existing dark editor tooling. New surfaces (landing, marketing) follow this rule; do not restyle the whole editor to match landing unless asked.
